  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Tabasco**: back after 212 archived shows (3875 days); rare: 9 archived performances [3]\n- **Red Baron**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [3]\n- **What You See Is What You Get**: back after 36 archived shows (514 days); rare: 3 archived performances [3]\n- **I Love You More Than You'll Ever Know**: back after 45 archived shows (684 days); rare: 3 archived performances [3]\n- **Boozer**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 5 archived performances [3]\n- **Hip Hug Her**: earliest performance in the archive; mythic rare: 2 archived performances [3]\n- **Never In All My Days**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [3]\n- **Hear My Train A Comin'**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [3]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **soulive2012-02-28.mk21.flac24** (recommended): audience recording; 14 songs; 164 min [1]\n- **soulive2012-02-28.mk21.flac16**: audience recording; 14 songs; 164 min [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- John Scofield sat in on guitar and Nigel Hall sang with the band on some songs [1]\n- Luther Dickinson guested on guitar, and James Casey played tambourine on some songs [1]\n- John Scofield sat in on guitar and Nigel Hall sang with the band on some songs [2]\n- Luther Dickinson guested on guitar, and James Casey played tambourine on some songs [2]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **soulive2012-02-28.mk21.flac24**: taped by Eric McRoberts; transferred by Eric McRoberts; source: Audience/On Stage [1]. Also: This is a 24-bit recording, not meant for MP3 streaming or CD burning; a CD-quality version also exists [1]\n- **soulive2012-02-28.mk21.flac16**: taped by Eric McRoberts; transferred by Eric McRoberts; source: Audience/On Stage [2]. Also: This is the CD-quality 16-bit version of the recording; a higher-quality 24-bit version also exists [2]",
